  "step_2": "The individual states that 'Prozent zahlen sind fast gleich, deshalb habe ich mich für 100 Euro mehr entschieden' which translates to 'The percentages are almost the same, so I chose the one with 100 Euros more.' This indicates that the individual perceives the probabilities as very similar and bases the choice on the higher monetary amount (2500 vs. 2400 Euros), not on the probability differences. The deliberation process emphasizes the monetary difference rather than the probability difference. There is no mention of comparing or weighing the probabilities, nor is there any justification based on preferring a higher probability of a favorable outcome.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the comparison of probabilities (34% vs. 33%) — is not considered by the individual. Instead, the individual focuses on the monetary difference (100 Euros more) and downplays the probability difference, stating they are 'almost the same.' The justification provided does not reflect the rule of the decision reason, which requires emphasizing the higher probability of a favorable outcome. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning is based on a different criterion (monetary gain), not on probability differences.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
